# WebQuark UI guidance

Use WebQuark for reusable UI primitives before creating custom replacements.
The shared boundary is `{webquark.foundationRoot}` and integration is
`{webquark.integrationEnabled}`.

## Working rules

1. Check the component catalogue below and its version-matched public API.
2. Prefer direct `q-*` custom elements. A standalone Angular component using them must declare `CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA`.
3. For compact desktop interfaces, use `size="sm"` when that component documents a public size option.
4. Put application-wide `--q-*` values only in `{webquark.foundationRoot}/styles/webquark-theme.css`.
5. Prefer theme tokens for global changes. Use documented Shadow Parts only for isolated exceptions.
6. Keep reusable wrappers and shared exceptions under `{webquark.foundationRoot}`; create them only when they add reusable project meaning, composition, or behavior.
7. Never style private shadow DOM or internal implementation classes.
8. If WebQuark has no suitable component, record the gap. Prefer accessible native HTML for a small gap before adding another UI library.

## Available components

- Actions: `q-button`, `q-chip`, `q-link`
- Layout and navigation: `q-card`, `q-carousel`, `q-form`, `q-navbar`, `q-panel`, `q-scrollable`, `q-sidepanel`, `q-toolbar`
- Forms: `q-input`, `q-textarea`, `q-dropdown`, `q-quantity-selector`, `q-radio-group`, `q-toggle`
- Data and indicators: `q-conversation-bubble`, `q-data-table`, `q-map`, `q-syntax-box`, `q-circular-progress`, `q-step-diagram`, `q-step-diagram-item`
- Media: `q-avatar`, `q-icon`, `q-reel`, `q-thumbnail`
- Overlays: `q-dialog`, `q-toast`, `q-tooltip`

Use WebQuark's `docs/components/README.md` for discovery, the matching
`docs/components/q-*.md` guide for intended use, generated
`src/components/**/readme.md` and installed TypeScript declarations for the
public contract, and `docs/theme_variables.md` for tokens. Generated API and
the installed declarations are authoritative. Canonical source:
<https://github.com/Purely-IT/WebQuark>.
